# Smart Motorcycle Accident Detection System (SafeRide)

An IoT-based real-time motorcycle accident detection and emergency response system built using an ESP32 microcontroller, MPU6050 IMU sensor, Touch Sensors, and NEO-M8N GPS module.

---

## Features
* Accident Detection Logic: Combines handle grip status (via touch sensors) and sudden impact detection (via MPU6050 accelerometer) to accurately identify crashes.
* Real-time GPS Tracking: Integrates a high-precision NEO-M8N GPS module with an external ceramic antenna to fetch precise emergency coordinates (Latitude & Longitude).
* Object-Oriented Programming (OOP): Modular C++ class design implemented via PlatformIO for clean and maintainable firmware.
* Serial Telemetry: Live status monitoring (Normal riding vs. Accident state with GPS coordinates) via Serial Monitor.

---

## Hardware Components
* Microcontroller: ESP32 Development Board
* Motion Sensor: MPU6050 6-axis Accelerometer & Gyroscope
* GPS Module: u-blox NEO-M8N (with External Ceramic Antenna)
* Touch Sensors: Handlebar Touch Sensors (Left & Right)
* Connectivity: Jumper wires, Breadboard / Custom PCB

---

## Pinout & Connections

| Component | Sensor Pin | ESP32 Pin |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| MPU6050 | SDA | GPIO 21 |
| MPU6050 | SCL | GPIO 22 |
| MPU6050 / GPS | VCC / GND | 3.3V / 5V & Common GND |
| Left Touch | SIG | GPIO 4 |
| Right Touch | SIG | GPIO 5 |
| NEO-M8N GPS | TX | GPIO 16 (RX2) |
| NEO-M8N GPS | RX | GPIO 17 (TX2) |

---

## Software & Libraries
Developed using PlatformIO with the Arduino framework. 

Required libraries (`lib_deps` in `platformio.ini`):
* `mikalhart/TinyGPSPlus` (v1.0.3 or higher)
* `electroniccats/MPU6050` (v0.6.0 or higher)

---

## Code Structure
* `MotionDetector` (C++ Class): Handles MPU6050 initialization and vibration threshold calculations.
* `TouchDetector` (C++ Class): Monitors handlebar grip states.
* `GpsSensor` (C++ Class): Manages UART communication and location parsing via TinyGPSPlus.
* `main.cpp`: Core logic loop combining sensor fusion and emergency state triggers.